# PART 1 — CORE LEARNING AND STUDY MECHANICS

## 1. Personalized Study Session and Time-Adaptive Scheduling

When a student enters the application, initially ask:

"How much uninterrupted time do you have available to study right now?"

Allow options such as:
- 20 minutes.
- 30 minutes.
- 45 minutes.
- 60 minutes.
- 90 minutes.
- 120 minutes.
- Custom duration.

The AI Personal Study Assistant should automatically generate a realistic study schedule based on the available time.

The schedule should include:
- Topics and subtopics.
- Lecture durations.
- Concept-learning activities.
- Practice questions.
- Flashcards.
- Quizzes.
- Revision activities.
- Short breaks.

Never generate a schedule that exceeds the available time.

Students should be able to modify the schedule before starting.

## 2. AI-Generated Micro-Lectures

Divide every topic into logical subtopics.

Each lecture must be no longer than 20 minutes.

If a concept requires more time, divide it into multiple independent lectures.

Every lecture should include:
- Simple conceptual explanations.
- Practical examples.
- Real-world applications.
- Diagrams and animations.
- Important formulas.
- Definitions.
- Examination-oriented concepts.
- Transcripts.

The platform should provide customized explanations according to the student's academic level.

